# 3. `filter()`

The `filter()` method creates a new array containing only the elements that satisfy a condition.

### Syntax

```javascript
array.filter(callback);
```

---

## 🔹 Basic Example

```javascript
const numbers = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6];

const evenNumbers = numbers.filter(number => number % 2 === 0);

console.log(evenNumbers);
```

Output:

```text
[2, 4, 6]
```

---

## 🔹 Filtering Objects

```javascript
const users = [
    { name: "Abhinav", age: 20 },
    { name: "Arun", age: 16 },
    { name: "Rahul", age: 25 }
];

const adults = users.filter(user => user.age >= 18);

console.log(adults);
```

Output:

```text
[
    { name: "Abhinav", age: 20 },
    { name: "Rahul", age: 25 }
]
```

---

## 🔹 Filter by Property

```javascript
const products = [
    { name: "Laptop", price: 60000 },
    { name: "Mouse", price: 1000 },
    { name: "Keyboard", price: 2000 }
];

const expensiveProducts = products.filter(
    product => product.price > 5000
);

console.log(expensiveProducts);
```

Output:

```text
[
    { name: "Laptop", price: 60000 }
]
```

### 🧠 Remember

```text
filter()
   ↓
Check condition
   ↓
Keep matching items
   ↓
New array
```

---

# 4. `find()`

The `find()` method returns the **first element** that satisfies a condition.

### Syntax

```javascript
array.find(callback);
```

---

## 🔹 Basic Example

```javascript
const numbers = [5, 10, 15, 20];

const result = numbers.find(number => number > 10);

console.log(result);
```

Output:

```text
15
```

Although `20` also matches, `find()` returns only the **first matching value**.

---

## 🔹 Finding an Object

```javascript
const users = [
    { id: 1, name: "Abhinav" },
    { id: 2, name: "Arun" },
    { id: 3, name: "Rahul" }
];

const user = users.find(user => user.id === 2);

console.log(user);
```

Output:

```text
{ id: 2, name: "Arun" }
```

---

## 🔹 When No Match Exists

```javascript
const numbers = [1, 2, 3];

const result = numbers.find(number => number > 10);

console.log(result);
```

Output:

```text
undefined
```

### 🧠 Remember

```text
find()
  ↓
Search
  ↓
First matching item
  ↓
Single value
```

